    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email-uniqueness rejection for owner creation, returning **409 Conflict** when an owner's lower-cased email is already used by another owner.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` pattern), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 the pipeline step. It reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes a lower-cased/trimmed comparison key, and iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()`. A matching key on any *other* owner throws `DuplicateEmailException`. An absent (null/blank) email is skipped \u2014 not a conflict.\n\n2. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 turns the exception into a 409 `ProblemDetail` response, matching the sibling handlers.\n\n4. **`...DuplicateEmailException.yml`** (`officefloor/escalation/`) \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n5. Inserted a **`checkEmail`** step into `owners.POST.yml` (after `checkTelephone`, before `checkHousehold`), governed by `transaction` like its neighbors.\n\nNote: `BuildOwner` already normalizes emails to lower-case on the way in, and the check lower-cases both sides defensively, so the comparison is case-insensitive as specified. The new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
